course: dictionary
lesson: 5473
title: Big words from the body
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A larynx is a noun, a naming word for a part of the body. It is your voice box, in your throat at the top of the windpipe. Science books use the word larynx because the voice box has its own special name.
explain: Inside the larynx are the vocal cords. Air from your lungs passes them, and they vibrate, which means they shake very quickly, to make a sound. Your mouth and tongue then shape that sound into words. «Your voice is made when air from the lungs passes the vocal cords in the voice box, the larynx, making them vibrate.»
explain: Look at the clue in that sentence. The words «the voice box» come right before «the larynx», so the two names mean the same part. This is a context clue: the writer explains the hard word for you.
fact: The larynx is the voice box, at the top of the windpipe in your throat.
fact: The vocal cords inside the larynx vibrate to make sounds.
fact: The larynx also helps stop food going into your lungs when you swallow.
fact: The plural of larynx can be larynges or larynxes.
fact: Laryngitis is an illness that makes you lose your voice.
exercise: What is the larynx? | A type of musical instrument | A part of the stomach that digests food | *The voice box at the top of the windpipe | A bone in your foot
exercise: What do the vocal cords do inside the larynx? | They store food | They hold your eyes in place | They pump blood round the body | *They vibrate to make sound
exercise: In «Your voice is made when air from the lungs passes the vocal cords in the voice box, the larynx», which words explain what the larynx is? | vibrate | lungs | *voice box | Your
test: What helps stop food going into the lungs when you swallow? | The eyes | The heart | The stomach | *The larynx
test: Laryngitis is an illness that makes you what? | *Lose your voice | Grow taller | Hear better | Lose your hair
exam: Which of these is a correct plural of larynx? | larynxs | larynxies | *larynxes | larynxx
